  bearers: [{"typicalBearer":"OWNER_OPERATOR","note":"Liner container shipping is dominated by vertically integrated carriers (Maersk, MSC, CMA CGM, COSCO, Hapag-Lloyd, ONE, Evergreen, HMM, ZIM, Yang Ming) that own/control tonnage and bunker purchasing directly; typical."},{"typicalBearer":"OWNER_OPERATOR","note":"Ferry/ro-pax operators (DFDS, Stena, Grimaldi, Attica Group, Tallink, etc.) typically own and directly operate their tonnage on fixed routes; typical."},{"typicalBearer":"MIXED","note":"Pure ro-ro tonnage spans owner-operated short-sea services and vessels time-chartered into car-carrier/forest-product pools; no single typical bearer."},{"typicalBearer":"OWNER_OPERATOR","note":"As with Passenger ship: cruise brands are vertically integrated owner-operators; typical."},{"typicalBearer":"TIME_CHARTERER","note":"General cargo/multipurpose tonnage trades tramp-style, typically time- or voyage-chartered; typical."},{"typicalBearer":"TIME_CHARTERER","note":"Tanker tonnage is predominantly chartered out (time or voyage) to oil majors/traders who control bunkering; under time charter the charterer bears fuel and FuelEU cost per BIMCO's clause; typical."},{"typicalBearer":"TIME_CHARTERER","note":"Chemical tankers trade on similar tramp/COA chartering patterns to oil tankers; typical."},{"typicalBearer":"OWNER_OPERATOR","note":"ConRo tonnage is generally deployed on owner-operated liner-type services (e.g. Grimaldi, ACL); typical."},{"typicalBearer":"MIXED","note":"LNG carriers are usually fixed on long-term time charters to energy majors/traders (who as charterer would bear FuelEU cost under the BIMCO clause), but many run on cargo boil-off gas supplied by the cargo owner, blurring who 'bears' the marine fuel cost; treated as mixed rather than a clean default."},{"typicalBearer":"TIME_CHARTERER","note":"Dry bulk is a tramp trade dominated by time/voyage chartering; under BIMCO's FuelEU Time Charter Clause the time charterer, who supplies bunkers, bears FuelEU compliance cost/strategy choices; typical."},{"typicalBearer":"MIXED","note":"Pure car/truck carriers (PCTC) split between owner-operators with captive OEM cargo (e.g. Wallenius Wilhelmsen, Eukor, Hoegh, NYK/MOL/K Line car-carrier arms) and tonnage time-chartered to OEMs/trading houses; no single typical bearer."},{"typicalBearer":"TIME_CHARTERER","note":"LPG/gas carriers below LNG scale are largely time-chartered to gas traders/majors who bunker the vessel; typical."},{"typicalBearer":"TIME_CHARTERER","note":"Reefer vessels are typically time-chartered into seasonal fruit/produce trades by charterers who supply bunkers; typical."},{"typicalBearer":"MIXED","note":"Catch-all MRV category covering heterogeneous vessel types with no single typical chartering pattern."},{"typicalBearer":"OWNER_OPERATOR","note":"Cruise and coastal-passenger operators (Carnival, RCG, NCLH, MSC Cruises, TUI Cruises, Hurtigruten, etc.) own/control their vessels directly; typical."},{"typicalBearer":"MIXED","note":"Combination/OBO carriers are a small, heterogeneous segment trading across both bulk and tanker charter markets; no single typical bearer."}],
